# Starlight Project Rules

This is a Space Station 14 content fork (Starlight). Follow upstream SS14/Robust Toolbox ECS architecture and the Starlight-specific placement rules below.

**Do not edit `RobustToolbox/`.** It is a separate engine project (read-only submodule). All work belongs in Starlight content; see `robust-toolbox-readonly.mdc`.

## Starlight File Placement

### New original content — put it in Starlight folders

All **new** Starlight code and assets belong under Starlight folder structures, mirroring existing layout:

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| Server systems | `Content.Server/_Starlight/` or `Content.Server/_Starlight/` |
| Shared components, events, systems | `Content.Shared/_Starlight/` |
| Client systems, UI | `Content.Client/_Starlight/` or `Content.Client/_Starlight/` |
| YAML prototypes | `Resources/Prototypes/_Starlight/` |
| Maps | `Resources/Maps/**/_Starlight/` |
| Textures / audio | `Resources/Textures/**/_Starlight/`, `Resources/Audio/**/_Starlight/` as appropriate |

Organize by feature (e.g. `Content.Server/_Starlight/Farts/FartSystem.cs`, `Content.Shared/_Starlight/Farts/FartComponent.cs`). Use file-scoped namespaces matching the folder path (e.g. `namespace Content.Server.Starlight.Farts;`).

Do **not** add new standalone features as loose files outside Starlight paths.

### Editing upstream files — mark every change with `//Starlight`

When modifying **existing** files that are **not** inside a Starlight subfolder, annotate every changed line or block:

**Single-line change** — append `//Starlight` (optional short note):

```csharp
using Content.Server.Starlight.Chat; //Starlight
public int Range { get; private set; } = 6; //Starlight: 10>6 to reduce spam
```

**Multi-line block** — wrap with begin/end comments:

```csharp
//Starlight - Begin
public void SetYield(SeedData seed, int newYield)
{
    seed.Yield = newYield;
}
//Starlight - End
```

Also acceptable: `//Starlight Block start` / `//Starlight block end`, or descriptive variants like `//Starlight - CyberMed Start`.

Apply the same rule to YAML edits in non-Starlight prototype files when adding or changing Starlight content inline.

Files already under `Starlight/` or `_Starlight/` paths do **not** need these markers.

